# 🔧 Network Troubleshooting Method

When a computer has no Internet connection, I can troubleshoot step-by-step:

```text
Check physical/Wi-Fi connection
          ↓
Check IP configuration
          ↓
Ping localhost
          ↓
Ping default gateway
          ↓
Ping external IP
          ↓
Test DNS resolution
          ↓
Trace network route
          ↓
Check ports/connections
```

### Example

#### Step 1 — Check IP configuration

```cmd
ipconfig /all
```

Check:

* IP address
* Subnet mask
* Default gateway
* DNS server

#### Step 2 — Test local TCP/IP stack

```cmd
ping 127.0.0.1
```

#### Step 3 — Test default gateway

```cmd
ping <gateway-ip>
```

#### Step 4 — Test Internet connectivity

```cmd
ping 8.8.8.8
```

#### Step 5 — Test DNS

```cmd
nslookup google.com
```

#### Step 6 — Trace the route

```cmd
tracert google.com
```

#### Step 7 — Check connections

```cmd
netstat -ano
```

